powerpc/powernv/eeh: do not make an EEH PE for NVLink NPU devices that have no PE yet (7.x)

EEH probes a device when it is added; the restored NVLink code assigns NPU PEs later, in
pnv_pci_ioda_setup_nvlink(). The EEH PE therefore carries IODA_INVALID_PE (PHB#7-PE#ffffffff), and a config
read that returns all-ones (a plain lspci) is treated as a frozen PE, cannot be recovered and ends in
'permanent failure', removing all twelve NPU link devices. Seen on 7.2.9-npu, 2026-10-04.
Local build for the AC922.

--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/eeh-powernv.c	2026-10-03 04:43:16.000000000 -0600
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/eeh-powernv.c	2026-10-04 21:04:17.782816077 -0600
@@ -350,6 +350,17 @@
 	if ((pdev->class >> 8) == PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_ISA)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * AC922 / NVLink local change: the emulated NPU link devices get their
+	 * PE later, from pnv_pci_ioda_setup_nvlink(). An EEH PE made now would
+	 * carry IODA_INVALID_PE, and the first config read returning all-ones
+	 * (any lspci) would be taken for a frozen PE, fail to recover and
+	 * remove every NPU device. Leave them out of EEH.
+	 */
+	if (phb->type == PNV_PHB_NPU_NVLINK &&
+	    phb->ioda.pe_rmap[config_addr] == IODA_INVALID_PE)
+		return NULL;
+
 	eeh_edev_dbg(edev, "Probing device\n");
 
 	/* Initialize eeh device */
